architecture : mirrors the sibling com/teslasync/battery/BatteryHealthPage + com/teslasync/analytics/StatisticsPage A7 precedent —
               framework-free Model (decode/derive/prefs, off-device testable), Source seam (cache-then-network Resource feeds +
               production binding over shared S8 SettingsStore + app-scoped SelectedVehicleStore + page-local SleepExtrasRepository
               CachingRepository on CacheDomain.Analytics over the shared ApiHttpClient + CacheStore), ViewModel (BaseFeedViewModel
               projecting Resource -> UiState via asUiState, displayPrefs StateFlow), stateless Page (entry constructs the VM,
               records the one-shot view.opened diagnostic, collects the feed + prefs; content draws the panels). The view performs
               NO HTTP. package io.teslasync.android.battery.sleepefficiency (dir com/teslasync/battery; InvalidPackageDeclaration
               suppressed exactly as the sibling surfaces).
data sources : useSleepEfficiency -> GET /analytics/sleep [vehicle_id, days] (web hook name kept at the call site; default window
               SLEEP_DEFAULT_DAYS=30 = web useRangeState '30d' preset). Settings (useUnits/useFormatting) + selected vehicle
               (useSelectedVehicle) from the shared holders.
si/units     : SI read off the wire; event outside temperatures are SI Celsius -> display via convertTempFromSI (prefs.fromCelsius)
               at the render boundary only; sentry energy (kWh) + costs render verbatim (web parity). No °F stored or computed.
states       : the sleep feed is the gate — loading (PageLoader) / error (ErrorDisplay+retry) / empty (EmptyState, hasData=false on a
               no-object / no-vehicle payload, web `sleep ? … : <noData>`) / success (the 8 panels). The two charts each render their
               own Ready/Empty surface (noStateData / noSentryData) and the table its own empty (noDrainEvents) so no section is hidden.
a11y/theme   : both charts carry accessibleDescription (the web aria-labels); the scope picker carries the sleep.selectVehicle
               contentDescription; the impact + table icons are decorative (contentDescription=null); colors via ChartPalette
               (paletteColor) + TeslaTokens.status/chart (A2 tokens) + MaterialTheme — dynamic color + dark theme; typography via the
               role components (PageTitle/SectionTitle/BodyText/Caption + MetricCard's MetricValue/MetricLabel). Compose-native donut
               (Canvas drawArc) + Vico BarChartWrapper — never a webview.
nav          : Destinations 'sleepEfficiency' -> /sleep-efficiency pre-existing (Destinations.kt L87, count unchanged); host wired via
               PageHosts.register("sleepEfficiency"); deep link auto-registered by the NavHost. DataContainer untouched.

